  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Tarok Romanian. Logic: Declarer's team needs 36+ card points; follow suit, must trump if unable; bid doi/unu/solo, call king, announcements then 12 tricks.",
    Player: 'Romanian Tarok is a point-trick game played mainly around Suceava in Moldavia. Introduced from Austria in the 19th century; uses 54-card Austrian tarok pack (22 trumpsâ€”taroaceâ€”plus four suits of eight). Highest trump skiz, then luna (XXI), lowest trump (I). Card values: skiz, luna, lowest trump and Kings 5, Queens 4, horses 3, Jacks 2, others 1. Objective: win tricks with valuable cards. Follow suit; must trump if unable. Cards in tricks counted in groups of three with 2 points subtracted per group. Phases: deal, bidding, calling a king, talon use, trick play, bonuses, declarations. Three-player variant Taper and other regional forms exist.',
    objective: "Declarer's team wins the hand by taking at least 36 card points in tricks (70 points total in the pack). Opponents win with 35 or more. Card points are counted in groups of three with 2 points subtracted per group.",
    gameplay: "1. Deal: Six cards to talon, 12 to each player in batches of 6; deal anticlockwise.\n2. Bidding: Player to dealer's right speaks first. Bids are unul de doi (take two from talon), unul de unu (take one), or solo (no talon). Pass allowed. Bidding continues until three players have passed.\n3. Call king: Declarer must call a king; its holder is declarer's partner (secret until revealed in play). Declarer may call a king they hold (play alone) or if the called king is in the talon (play alone).\n4. Talon: In doi declarer takes two cards from talon and discards two; in unu takes one and discards one; in solo talon stays unseen. Kings, skiz, luna and lowest trump (I) cannot be discarded.\n5. Announcements: Declarer speaks first, then anticlockwise. Players may declare trump count (8, 9, or 10+ taroace) and announce bonuses (trula, trump-I-ultimo, rege ultimo, valat, etc.); contra and recontra apply.\n6. Play: Player to dealer's right leads. Follow suit; must play a tarok if unable to follow; if tarok is led, must play tarok if possible. Trick won by highest tarok, or highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Twelve tricks.\n7. Scoring: Each team counts card points in tricks won; declarer's team needs 36+ to win the game. Bonuses (trula, trump-I-ultimo, etc.) scored per payment table.",
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit; must play a tarok if you cannot follow suit.',
      'If a tarok is led, you must play a tarok if you can.',
      'Trick is won by the highest tarok in it, or if no tarok, by the highest card of the suit led.',
      "Declarer's team needs at least 36 of 70 card points to win the game.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
