    turnFlow: "1. Deal: Six cards to talon, 12 to each player in batches of 6; deal anticlockwise.\n2. Bidding: Player to dealer's right speaks first. Bids are unul de doi (take two from talon), unul de unu (take one), or solo (no talon). Pass allowed. Bidding continues until three players have passed.\n3. Call king: Declarer must call a king; its holder is declarer's partner (secret until revealed in play). Declarer may call a king they hold (play alone) or if the called king is in the talon (play alone).\n4. Talon: In doi declarer takes two cards from talon and discards two; in unu takes one and discards one; in solo talon stays unseen. Kings, skiz, luna and lowest trump (I) cannot be discarded.\n5. Announcements: Declarer speaks first, then anticlockwise. Players may declare trump count (8, 9, or 10+ taroace) and announce bonuses (trula, trump-I-ultimo, rege ultimo, valat, etc.); contra and recontra apply.\n6. Play: Player to dealer's right leads. Follow suit; must play a tarok if unable to follow; if tarok is led, must play tarok if possible. Trick won by highest tarok, or highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Twelve tricks.\n7. Scoring: Each team counts card points in tricks won; declarer's team needs 36+ to win the game. Bonuses (trula, trump-I-ultimo, etc.) scored per payment table.",
